# aggregator-fold

The aggregation-algebra hot path (`specs/aggregation-algebra.md`): a `prepare`/`combine` fold
through a `Monoid` dictionary with a TUPLE accumulator (the `ZipAgg(SumAgg, CountAgg)` shape —
one pass, two answers), plus a `groupByAgg`-style keyed fold through `Map.updated`/`getOrElse`.
Stresses trait-method dispatch through a typeclass value, per-element tuple allocation, and
Map churn under a keyed aggregation — the exact costs `runAggregator`/`groupByAgg` pay per
element in production use. Self-contained mirror of `std/aggregator.ssc`'s shapes (bench corpus
entries do not import modules); keep the shapes in sync with the spec if they change there.

```scalascript
trait Monoid2[A]:
  def empty: A
  def combine(a: A, b: A): A

class PairSumCount() extends Monoid2[(Long, Long)]:
  def empty: (Long, Long) = (0L, 0L)
  def combine(a: (Long, Long), b: (Long, Long)): (Long, Long) =
    (a._1 + b._1, a._2 + b._2)

def workload(): Long =
  val m = PairSumCount()
  // zip-shaped fold: sum + count in one pass over 1000 elements
  var acc = m.empty
  var i = 0
  while i < 1000 do
    acc = m.combine(acc, (i.toLong, 1L))
    i = i + 1
  // groupBy-shaped keyed fold: 1000 elements into a 10-key Map
  var groups: Map[Int, Long] = Map[Int, Long]()
  var j = 0
  while j < 1000 do
    val k = j % 10
    groups = groups.updated(k, groups.getOrElse(k, 0L) + j.toLong)
    j = j + 1
  acc._1 + acc._2 + groups.getOrElse(3, 0L)
```
